        "Stage 2: Neural Detection & Localization: The test tensor X_test is passed through the YOLO11n object detector backbone, yielding a set of M candidate defect detections: D = { (b_k, c_k, p_k) }_{k=1}^M, where b_k = [x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max] represents the normalized bounding box coordinates, c_k in {1, ..., 6} denotes the predicted defect class, and p_k in [0, 1] represents the raw neural confidence logit.",
        "Stage 3: Sub-pixel Registration & Mask Generation: For each detected bounding box b_k, a local region of interest (ROI) is extracted from both X_test and X_ref with a 10-pixel spatial padding. The ROI tensors are binarized via adaptive Otsu thresholding to yield binary copper masks B_test and B_ref. A morphological dilation operator with structuring element radius delta_reg = 2 pixels is applied to absorb mechanical conveyor jitter, generating a noise-tolerant differential mask M_diff.",
        "Stage 4: Topological Graph Consequence Extraction: The binary masks are skeletonized using the Zhang-Suen thinning algorithm to produce 1-pixel-wide medial axes. Connected component analysis and graph traversal algorithms construct planar graphs G_test = (V_t, E_t) and G_ref = (V_r, E_r). By evaluating topological invariants (Euler characteristic, component count Delta N_comp, and cut-vertices), the consequence engine outputs binary functional hazard indicators: I_break in {0, 1} and I_bridge in {0, 1}.",
        "Stage 5: Conformal Scoring & Queue Routing: A compound non-conformity score S_k = S(p_k, I_break, I_bridge, c_k) is computed for each candidate defect. The score is evaluated against calibrated empirical quantiles (q_hat_pass, q_hat_reject) computed during split-conformal calibration. The system emits a structured JSON payload containing the final queue assignment: Q_k in {AUTO_PASS, MANUAL_REVIEW, AUTO_REJECT}, accompanied by bounding box coordinates, class labels, and visual overlay telemetry."
