        "S_B(x) = (1 - p_k) + lambda_1 * I_break + lambda_2 * I_bridge + lambda_3 * (1 - d_clear / d_nominal)",
        "where lambda_1 = 2.0, lambda_2 = 2.0, and lambda_3 = 0.5 are hyperparameter weights calibrated on validation data. This formulation heavily penalizes true functional circuit hazards, driving their non-conformity scores into the extreme upper tail of the calibration distribution, thereby guaranteeing their routing to immediate reject or manual review queues while allowing benign cosmetic anomalies to be safely cleared."
