        "In industrial SMT deployment, an inspection system trained on existing board layouts must immediately inspect completely novel board designs with different routing geometries, copper densities, and surface finishes, without requiring costly per-board model retraining or manual recalibration. Standard k-fold cross-validation fails to simulate this scenario because random folds contain mixed crops from all boards.",
        "The LOBO protocol executes 11 exhaustive cross-fitting iterations. In each iteration k in {1, ..., 11}, all image crops originating from Board_k are completely isolated as the unseen test set, while the remaining 10 boards form the training and calibration sets. Across all 11 folds, the neural detector is trained, Consequence Engine v3 extracts topological features, and the conformal calibrator calculates thresholds on the training boards. Performance metrics—empirical escape rate M_crit, review load reduction R_load, and quality cost E[C_Q]—are evaluated strictly on the held-out board. This protocol guarantees zero board-level data leakage and provides an authoritative assessment of model robustness against real-world manufacturing distribution shifts."
